                <pb facs="0567" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg493"/>

                <head>No. 5.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—<placeName>Madrid</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-14">February 14</date>—3 1/2
                        o’clock p. m,]</dateline></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Official service.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Chargé d’Affaires of the United States,
                        Paris:</hi></p>
                <p>A blockade-runner steamer under English flag has entered Ferrol with men,
                    ammunition, and supplies for the Stonewall. This ship will be ready to sail
                    to-day. The Niagara is vigilant. The Sacramento is still at Lisbon, in spite of
                    all my efforts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PERRY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
